    analysis:[{t:"Requirements consolidation",d:"Interviewed 10+ mechanical engineers and collapsed conflicting quality requirements and reporting milestones into a single measurement approach design, quality, and manufacturing could all sign."},{t:"Seating on a surface with no datum",d:"An airfoil has no flat face to register against, so the gauge body carries the contour itself and locates on the part rather than on a fixture. Concave and convex sides get separate bodies because one shape cannot seat correctly on both."},{t:"Go / no-go instead of a reading",d:"Pairing each gauge with a go / no-go pin converts a measurement into a decision. The technician does not interpret a number against a spec, which removes operator judgement from the accept step and makes the result auditable."},{t:"Fabrication route per part",d:"Some gauges are machined and some printed, chosen against geometry, quantity, lead time, and how much abuse the tool takes in service rather than by defaulting to one process for the family."},{t:"Supplier and floor integration",d:"Quoted and managed the outside fabrication, then took the tooling onto the floor \u2014 fitting it to real hardware, training against it, and writing it into standard work so it is the method rather than an option."}],
